# Deterministic whole-line reveal positions; source order and verse contents unchanged.
an3.30:7.1 starts: While sitting in his seat,
an3.30:7.2 none
an3.30:7.3 starts: he grasps the phrasing of the talk,
an3.30:7.4 starts: at its beginning, middle, and end.
an3.30:7.5 starts: But after rising, he no longer understands,
an3.30:7.6 starts: but forgets what he had learned.
an3.39:11.1 starts: having seen security in renunciation.
an3.39:11.2 none
an3.39:11.3 starts: “Zeal then arose in me
an3.39:11.4 starts: as I clearly saw nibbāna.
an4.60:4.1 starts: for them both by day and night
an4.60:4.2 none
an4.60:4.3 starts: merit always increases;
an4.60:4.4 none
an4.60:4.5 starts: having done excellent deeds,
an4.60:4.6 starts: they pass on to a heavenly state.
an5.57:15.1 starts: having seen security in renunciation.
an5.57:15.2 none
an5.57:15.3 starts: “Zeal then arose in me
an5.57:15.4 starts: as I clearly saw nibbāna.
sn22.76:5.1 starts: Limpid are their minds;
sn22.76:5.2 none
sn22.76:5.3 starts: They are unsullied in the world—
sn22.76:5.4 starts: The holy ones, without taints.
sn22.76:10.1 starts: They are released from renewed existence.
sn22.76:10.2 none
sn22.76:10.3 starts: Having reached the stage of the tamed,
sn22.76:10.4 starts: They are the victors in the world.
